@bernd-edlinger not any more than it is already broken
1. there is a non-insignificant chance that decrypting a random ciphertext will result in valid padding (and a valid ciphertext from one key looks like random ciphertext for a second key)
2. doesn't CMS_RecipientInfo_decrypt() actually decrypt the PKCS#1 ciphertext and then uses that to do the symmetric decryption (with something like AES-CBC)? So the PKCS#1 decryption not only has to provide a plaintext of expected size, it also needs to lead to symmetric decryption that has correct padding for the code to accept the key as correct?

